<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's budget deficit rose 1.2 pct Jan-Nov.</title>
<headline>Portugal's budget deficit rose 1.2 pct Jan-Nov.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's budget deficit widened 1.2 percent in the first 11 months of the year to 480.6 billion escudos, compared with the same period last year, the Finance Ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry said that the difference reflected changes in the method of accounting, with book profits on Treasury operations not being included this year.</p>
<p>The state deficit is forecast to narrow to some 4.0 percent of gross domestic product (GDP) in 1996 from around 4.9 percent a year ago.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the Jan-Nov budget figures in billions of escudos:</p>
<p>				  Jan-Nov 1996  Jan-Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Current receipts	 3,632.7	 3,343.8</p>
<p>	Direct taxes	   1,357.8	 1,180.1</p>
<p>	Indirect taxes	 1,961.4	 1,838.9</p>
<p>	Other receipts	   313.5	   324.8</p>
<p>    Current spending	 3,728.4	 3,519.4</p>
<p>Transfers to public</p>
<p>	administration	 1,219.7	   991.8</p>
<p>	Debt financing	   695.9	   734.1</p>
<p>    Balance		     -480.6	  -474.9</p>
<p>    Primary balance	    215.3	   259.2</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113126</p>
